# time.schema — who may set each key of the `time` subsystem (see w-conf.md).
# Format: <KEY>\t<scope>   scope: system | user | both
#
# The clock and its servers are system state — there is one system time, so a
# per-user override would be meaningless.
SERVERS	system
FALLBACK	system
# The server catalog is data the admin extends: a GLOB row declares the whole
# family at once, so a new entry is never silently unconstrained (a user file
# redefining NTP_google would otherwise redirect the machine's time source).
NTP_*	system
